Ladybird’s Error constructors capture the stack without their own
native frame; a subclass constructor’s frame stays. V8’s
ErrorUtils::Construct() captures with FrameSkipMode SKIP_FIRST, since
“the first frame is always a BUILTIN_EXIT frame” when the Error
constructor is called, and with SKIP_UNTIL_SEEN and new_target as the
caller for a subclass, which drops the subclass constructor’s frame
too (isolate.cc, StackFrameBuilder). JSC’s ErrorConstructor passes
useCurrentFrame = false to ErrorInstance::create(), and newTarget as
subclassCaller for subclasses, to the same effect. SpiderMonkey’s
CaptureStack() records only script frames in its SavedStacks, so a
native constructor frame never appears there at all.
